"AC4: 'can never read as affirmative evidence (unit test asserts wording)' — asserts wording only, not the resulting finalizer verdict"],"finding":"The plan claims the placeholder makes the finalizer 'score the criterion unmet/indeterminate, not met', but no acceptance criterion proves that scoring OUTCOME. AC4 only asserts the placeholder WORDING is non-affirmative; wording being non-affirmative does not prove the finalizer actually scores the exhausted criterion as unmet/indeterminate rather than accidentally met. This leaves the central safety claim (exhaustion is not an affirmative verdict) unverified end-to-end.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe714ab4ff90469a0","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (AC4) vs. Plan body 'so the finalizer scores the criterion unmet/indeterminate, not met'","norm_id":"nc34018293c24e15d","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A finalizer prompt/scorer that treats a present-but-content-free evidence entry as weak-positive could score the exhausted criterion 'met', re-creating the exhaustion-is-a-verdict trap this cluster removes"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add: 'Given a placeholder (exhausted=true) evidence entry, the finalizer's per-criterion verdict for that criterion is unmet/indeterminate — unit test asserts the structured verdict, not the placeholder text.'","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a deterministic backstop: after the finalizer returns, force any criterion whose evidence entry carries exhausted=true to met=false (or fail closed) rather than relying solely on placeholder wording + finalizer-LLM judgment, and cover it with a unit test that asserts the criterion is scored not-met even when the finalizer attempts met=true.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan relies on the finalizer LLM: 'so the finalizer scores the criterion unmet/indeterminate, not met'","completion_recovery.py:381 only rejects 'PASS verdict' when 'any(not record[\"met\"])' — it does NOT force any specific criterion to unmet","No code path ties an 'exhausted' evidence entry to met=false; search for 'exhausted' in the module finds only comments/messages, no scoring guard","AC line 4 asserts placeholder WORDING ('unit test asserts wording') but does not test that the finalizer actually scores the exhausted criterion as not-met — the safety property is left to LLM discretion"],"finding":"The plan's safety guarantee that an exhausted criterion is scored unmet/indeterminate (not met) rests entirely on placeholder wording plus the finalizer LLM's non-deterministic judgment; there is no deterministic backstop forcing an exhausted=true entry to met=false, so the finalizer could still mark it met and — since the existing guard at completion_recovery.py:381 only blocks PASS-with-unmet — pass a PASS verdict, reintroducing the exhaustion-is-not-a-verdict trap the cluster is meant to remove.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2b48f474789172ed","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Plan:' ('Placeholder text must never be presentable as affirmative evidence ... so the finalizer scores the criterion unmet/indeterminate, not met'); completion_recovery.py:_validate_coverage/PASS-guard (354-389)","norm_id":"n9a5abfd7adcf58aa","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["Finalizer LLM reads a content-free 'could-not-gather-within-bounds' placeholder and, mis-generalizing from surrounding met criteria, marks the exhausted criterion met=true; PASS verdict slips through since line 381 sees no unmet record","A future finalizer prompt revision subtly weakens exhausted-placeholder handling and silently regresses the safety property with no deterministic test catching it"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"In _recover, after _validate_coverage, cross-reference each finalizer record against the evidence list: for every criterion whose evidence entry has exhausted=true, assert/override record['met'] is False (raise CompletionRecoveryError if the finalizer returned met=true for an exhausted criterion). This makes the safety property deterministic instead of LLM-discretionary and complements the existing line-381 PASS-with-unmet guard.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_c